  "historical_output_text": " On a rainy afternoon, I decided to bake cookies with my niece. Her favorite are oatmeal raisin, so I picked up the recipe online. Following the instructions, I preheated the oven, measured the ingredients, and started mixing them in a large bowl. After combining the ingredients, I was so confident in my precision that I skipped the recipe's recommendation to let the dough rest for an hour.\n\nI immediately regretted this decision as soon as I dropped the dough onto the baking sheet. The first cookie was clearly too wet, and as I placed it into the oven, I noticed the edges were already starting to burn. My face turned red as I realized I should have followed the recipe more closely. Despite this mistake, I decided to press on and bake the rest of the cookies, which turned out fine.\n\nLater that night, my niece tasted the cookies, and while she liked them, she commented on how the edges were not as crisp as usual. Although disappointed, I couldn't help but feel a small sense of satisfaction. I had learned that adhering to a recipe can be important, especially when it comes to something as specific as baking times and dough",
